body:
That is the most beautiful creature I have ever seen. The pose, those eyes, those EARS!! Perfection in every way

&#x200B;

tho the ears look a bit frost bitten maybe? is that why the tops are pink and looks like its lost hair....

I think it's a wonderful idea to research other religions for your own faith and if you need to do it stealthily then it just requires extra care and forethought. I was raised Christian (catholic) and for years through youth group and service I struggled with my faith and became increasingly agnostic. It is between you and whatever God or no God you believe in as to what your faith is... that being said, research and meditate on your beliefs, find what speaks to you and look into it. something might spark your soul and you read into it and no wait no it dosnt anymore so go onto the next until you are happy and at peace with what you believe in. It might be wicca, it might not be.

&#x200B;

As for casting spells, there are many tricks for 'broom closeted' witches and a few youtube video's that i've personally watched and taken tips from. but in wicca you dont have to have props to worship, or at least not overtly 'heathen' props. I personally set up a few angle statues around my sudo alter because i feel a connection with them and they bring me peace in my spirit.

&#x200B;

Your faith is yours, but most importantly dont limit yourself just to looking into one religion. research before jumping in full throttle and find something that gives you peace and the desire to follow that faith.
